Rational Woman and Irrational Woman both buy new bikes, and they decide to drive around two racetracks from time $t = 0$ to $t = \infty.$ Rational Woman drives along the path parameterized by
\begin{align*}
x &= 2 + 2 \cos t, \\
y &= 1 + 2 \sin t,
\end{align*}
and Irrational Woman drives along the path parameterized by
\begin{align*}
x &= 3 + 3 \cos \frac{t}{2}, \\
y &= 2 + 3 \sin \frac{t}{2}.
\end{align*}
If $A$ is a point on Rational Woman's racetrack, and $B$ is a point on Irrational Woman's racetrack, then find the smallest possible distance $AB$.

