Since the sum of the angles in triangle $ABC$ is $180^\circ$ and we know two angles are $75^\circ$ and $30^\circ$, which add to $105^\circ$, then $\angle ACB = 180^\circ - 105^\circ = \boxed{75^\circ}$.

